## Classes
Classes are blueprints for creating objects. Instead of writing a function that returns an object, you define a class:

```ts
class User {
    name: string;
    age: number;

    constructor(name: string, age: number) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }
}

const user = new User("Steve", 25);
console.log(user.name);  // Steve
```

- `class` defines the blueprint
- `constructor` runs when you call `new`
- `this` refers to the object being created
- `new` creates an instance of the class

---
## Assignment:
Create a class `Video` with properties `title` (string), `views` (number), and `likes` (number). The constructor takes `title` and `views`, and sets `likes` to 0.

